C<trim-silence>.

=item C<wait_method>

The HTTP method we should use to call C<wait_url>. Can be C<GET> or C<POST> and
the default is C<POST>. When using a static audio file, this should be C<GET>
so that we can cache the file. One of C<GET> or C<POST>.

=item C<wait_url>

The URL that Twilio calls using the C<wait_method> before the conference has
started. The URL may return an MP3 file, a WAV file, or a TwiML document. The
default value is the URL of our standard hold music. If you do not want
anything to play while waiting for the conference to start, specify an empty
string by setting C<wait_url> to C<''>. For more details on the allowable verbs
within the C<waitUrl>, see the C<waitUrl> attribute in the
L<E<lt>ConferenceE<gt> TwiML
instruction|https://www.twilio.com/docs/voice/twiml/conference#attributes-waiturl>.

=back

=head2 read

  my @records = $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants->read(\%options, $limit, $page_size);

Retrieve a list of participants belonging to the account used to make the
request. Returns the records as a list, fetching as many pages as it needs.

The options are:

=over

=item C<coaching>

Whether to return only participants who are coaching another call. Can be:
C<true> or C<false>.

=item C<hold>

Whether to return only participants that are on hold. Can be: C<true> or
C<false>.

=item C<muted>

Whether to return only participants that are muted. Can be: C<true> or
C<false>.

=back

=head2 stream

  my $stream = $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants->stream(\%options, $limit, $page_size);

Takes the same arguments as L</read>, and returns a L<Twilio::Stream>.

=head2 page

  my $page = $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants->page(\%options, $page_size, $page_token, $page_number);

Fetches one page, and returns a L<Twilio::Page>.

=head2 get_page

  my $page = $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants->get_page($url);

Fetches the page at a URL given by Twilio.

=head2 get_context

  my $context = $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants->get_context($call_sid);

Returns a C<ParticipantContext>, and makes no request.

=head1 ParticipantPage

A L<Twilio::Page> of C<ParticipantInstance> objects.

=head2 records_key

=head2 build_instance

Used by L<Twilio::Page>.

=head1 ParticipantContext

Returned by C<< $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants($call_sid)
>>. It makes no request until one of these methods is called.

=head2 fetch

  my $participant = $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants($call_sid)->fetch;

Fetch an instance of a participant. Returns a C<ParticipantInstance>.

=head2 update

  my $participant = $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants($call_sid)->update(\%options);

Update the properties of the participant. Returns a C<ParticipantInstance>.

The options are:

=over

=item C<announce_method>

The HTTP method we should use to call C<announce_url>. Can be: C<GET> or
C<POST> and defaults to C<POST>. One of C<GET> or C<POST>.

=item C<announce_url>

The URL we call using the C<announce_method> for an announcement to the
participant. The URL may return an MP3 file, a WAV file, or a TwiML document
that contains C<< <Play> >>, C<< <Say> >>, C<< <Pause> >>, or C<< <Redirect> >>
verbs.

=item C<beep_on_exit>

Whether to play a notification beep to the conference when the participant
exits. Can be: C<true> or C<false>.

=item C<call_sid_to_coach>

The SID of the participant who is being C<coached>. The participant being
coached is the only participant who can hear the participant who is
C<coaching>.

=item C<coaching>

Whether the participant is coaching another call. Can be: C<true> or C<false>.
If not present, defaults to C<false> unless C<call_sid_to_coach> is defined. If
C<true>, C<call_sid_to_coach> must be defined.

=item C<end_conference_on_exit>

Whether to end the conference when the participant leaves. Can be: C<true> or
C<false> and defaults to C<false>.

=item C<hold>

Whether the participant should be on hold. Can be: C<true> or C<false>. C<true>
puts the participant on hold, and C<false> lets them rejoin the conference.

=item C<hold_method>

The HTTP method we should use to call C<hold_url>. Can be: C<GET> or C<POST>
and the default is C<GET>. One of C<GET> or C<POST>.

=item C<hold_url>

The URL we call using the C<hold_method> for music that plays when the
participant is on hold. The URL may return an MP3 file, a WAV file, or a TwiML
document that contains C<< <Play> >>, C<< <Say> >>, C<< <Pause> >>, or C<<
<Redirect> >> verbs.

=item C<muted>

Whether the participant should be muted. Can be C<true> or C<false>. C<true>
will mute the participant, and C<false> will un-mute them. Anything value other
than C<true> or C<false> is interpreted as C<false>.

=item C<wait_method>

The HTTP method we should use to call C<wait_url>. Can be C<GET> or C<POST> and
the default is C<POST>. When using a static audio file, this should be C<GET>
so that we can cache the file. One of C<GET> or C<POST>.

=item C<wait_url>

The URL that Twilio calls using the C<wait_method> before the conference has
started. The URL may return an MP3 file, a WAV file, or a TwiML document. The
default value is the URL of our standard hold music. If you do not want
anything to play while waiting for the conference to start, specify an empty
string by setting C<wait_url> to C<''>. For more details on the allowable verbs
within the C<waitUrl>, see the C<waitUrl> attribute in the
L<E<lt>ConferenceE<gt> TwiML
instruction|https://www.twilio.com/docs/voice/twiml/conference#attributes-waiturl>.

=back

=head2 delete

  $client->conferences($conference_sid)->participants($call_sid)->delete;

Kick a participant from a given conference. Returns true.

=head1 ParticipantInstance

See also L<Twilio::InstanceResource>.

It has C<fetch>, C<update> and C<delete>, which work as they do on the context.

Its fields are:

=over

=item account_sid

The SID of the L<Account|https://www.twilio.com/docs/iam/api/account> that
created the Participant resource.

=item call_sid

The SID of the L<Call|https://www.twilio.com/docs/voice/api/call-resource> the
Participant resource is associated with.

=item call_sid_to_coach

The SID of the participant who is being C<coached>. The participant being
coached is the only participant who can hear the participant who is
C<coaching>.

=item coaching

Whether the participant is coaching another call. Can be: C<true> or C<false>.
If not present, defaults to C<false> unless C<call_sid_to_coach> is defined. If
C<true>, C<call_sid_to_coach> must be defined.

=item conference_sid

The SID of the conference the participant is in.

=item date_created

The date and time in GMT that the resource was created specified in L<RFC
2822|https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2822.txt> format. A L<Time::Piece> object in
UTC. See L<Twilio::Deserialize/date_time>.

=item date_updated

The date and time in GMT that the resource was last updated specified in L<RFC
2822|https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc2822.txt> format. A L<Time::Piece> object in
UTC. See L<Twilio::Deserialize/date_time>.

=item end_conference_on_exit

Whether the conference ends when the participant leaves. Can be: C<true> or
C<false> and the default is C<false>. If C<true>, the conference ends and all
other participants drop out when the participant leaves.

=item hold

Whether the participant is on hold. Can be C<true> or C<false>.

=item label

The user-specified label of this participant, if one was given when the
participant was created. This may be used to fetch, update or delete the
participant.

=item muted

Whether the participant is muted. Can be C<true> or C<false>.

=item queue_time

The wait time in milliseconds before participant's call is placed. Only
available in the response to a create participant request.

=item start_conference_on_enter

Whether the conference starts when the participant joins the conference, if it
has not already started. Can be: C<true> or C<false> and the default is
C<true>. If C<false> and the conference has not started, the participant is
muted and hears background music until another participant starts the
conference.

=item status

One of C<queued>, C<connecting>, C<ringing>, C<connected>, C<complete> or
C<failed>.

=item uri

The URI of the resource, relative to C<https://api.twilio.com>.

=back

